here is one of the trained model for  minis image classification as a response  to the common criticism that Mechelen  models are not interpretable let's have  a closer look at the trained model  parameters each line here represents one  model parameter for all the parameters  connected to the one output we could  transform them into a 2d image for  example here is a 2d image for all the  model parameters connected to the first  output which represent the digit zero  here the yellow color represents the  weights have large values and the blue  color represents the weights have small  values the following figures shows the  weights visualization for each digit  from 0 to 9 it is pretty clear to see  how each figure highlights or activates  different parts of the images  corresponding to different digit classes  using this model for each input image in  the test dataset we can calculate the  luggage score of each digit class with  the linear weighted sum of the model  with W and input X in this way we can  classify the input image into one of the  classes with the highest luggage score  here  let's also record the prediction result  for each test image in a confusion  matrix for the first example we have the  input image as 8 and the prediction is 8  and for the second example we have the  input image as 5 and that the prediction  is 6 the confusion matrix is reputable  way of visualizing the performance of in  the image classification model each  entry in the confusion matrix denotes  the number of predictions that were made  by the models will it classify the image  correctly or incorrectly after iterating  through all the test data set we can  derive recall precision and f1 score for  each class here I will not dive deep  into how to calculate them where the  details can be found in our confusion  matrix video this is the code block to  do the evaluation  the results looks very good for these  simple classification problems with a  simple softmax regression model it is a  relatively easy task in image  classification in the future video we  will show you how to extend this model  and Papp line to solve more difficult  problems with more complicated models  such as convolutional neural network  don't forget to subscribe to us and rain  the notification bell and stay tuned
 

